{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And I will put.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel: See what the difference is between you and the nations of the world — when they sin, I first strike them and afterward their houses, as it is said: ״וינגע ה' את פרעה״ etc. But you — if you sin, I strike your houses first, as it is said: ״ונתתי נגע צרעת בבית ארץ אחוזתכם״. And what have the wood and stones sinned? Rather, so that they will see and take reproof. And so you find: when Israel sinned and the Holy One, blessed be He, wanted to exile them, He brought Sennacherib upon all the nations, so that Israel would see and repent, as it is said: ״הכרת גוים״ etc. Thus the Holy One, blessed be He, shows a person and strikes his house first; if he repents — well and good; and if not, his garments are stricken, as it is said afterward: ״ולצרעת הבגד״; and still, if he repented — well and good, and if not, he is stricken in his body, as it is said in the end: ״איש כי יהיה זב״; and he is also stricken in these three kinds: שאת and ספחת and לבהרת. And thus it says: ״נכונו וללצים שפטים״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: Before I created him I prepared these for him. Parable of a wicked servant who was sold in the market. A man went to buy him and recognized that he was wicked, and took with him chains and a rod to subdue him with if he rebelled. When he rebelled, he bound him in chains and struck him with the rod."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:17.461545417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}